---
>   2.048 s. U1/U2 are refused; suspend drops any pending snapshot and restarts
>   from a new baseline (bit 0 on the next reference, the sequence continuing).
>   With FX3 USB 2.0 fallback enabled, the pinned SDK does not raise
>   `USB3_LNKFAIL`: a SuperSpeed link failure arrives as fallback, reset or
>   disconnect, which disarm; the `USB3_LNKFAIL` and compliance-entry branches
>   are defensive (SDK 1.3.5 `fw_lib/1_3_5/inc/cyu3usb.h`, lines 146–155 and
>   1871–1892). Link Recovery leaves U0 without restarting the baseline; any
>   selected ITP it costs is caught by the count step (bit 0 on the next
>   reference), because Recovery is bounded far below 2.048 s
>   ([USB 3.2 §7.5](https://www.usb.org/document-library/usb-32-revision-11-june-2022),
>   including §7.5.10 Recovery; compliance entry is from Polling, §7.5.5).
>   Reset, disconnect and configuration changes disarm.
